data_pds2
# Phase identity: ambient orthorhombic PdS2-type PdS2, Pbca, Z=4.
# Provenance: Gronvold and Rost, Acta Cryst. 10, 329--331 (1957),
# COD 2310589 (CC0): https://www.crystallography.net/cod/2310589.cif
# This P1 representation explicitly expands Pd 4a and S 8c from the source.
# The weakly bonded layers are normal to (001). Pbca extinguishes odd 00l,
# so the catalog pins the first usable parallel reciprocal vector, (002).
# Limiting checks: V=abc, 4Pd+8S, and finite basal (002) coupling.
# Validation: pds2-pbca-structure
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M 'P 1'
_symmetry_Int_Tables_number 1
_cell_length_a 5.460
_cell_length_b 5.541
_cell_length_c 7.531
_cell_angle_alpha 90.0
_cell_angle_beta 90.0
_cell_angle_gamma 90.0
